        "content": "Drive time is pure cost: fuel burned and hours paid while no carpet is being cleaned, and a dispatch board is your main tool for minimizing it. When jobs are visible together with their locations, you can sequence a technician's day so appointments flow geographically instead of crisscrossing the service area. A board that ties into mapping shows you when a route doubles back wastefully, letting you reorder stops so the truck moves in a sensible arc rather than bouncing across town. For carpet cleaning, where a single day might span suburbs far apart, tightening routes recovers hours that convert directly into additional billable jobs. Grouping nearby appointments also creates the flexibility to slot in a same-day request without wrecking the schedule, because the technician is already in the area. The board turns route planning from a guess into a deliberate act. Every mile you cut is money kept, and across a full fleet over a season, disciplined routing off the dispatch board adds up to a substantial reduction in the cost of getting to the work."
